▌ src/auth/fingerprint.rs:42 · bug · conf 90                |
▌ Re-key drops sessions created during the migration window |
▌ The loop reads the old key once and writes the new one    |
▌ after every batch, so sessions created mid-run keep the   |
▌ old fingerprint.                                          |
▌ ▾ failure scenario                                        |
▌   A user logs in while the re-key runs; their next request|
▌   fails the fingerprint check and they are signed out.    |
▌ ▾ suggestion                                              |
▌   Take the write lock for the whole re-key, or re-read the|
▌   key per batch.                                          |
